course: dictionary
lesson: 323
title: Anglerfish: the fish with a fishing rod
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An anglerfish is a fish with a big mouth and sharp teeth that lives in the deep, dark ocean. It catches its food with a long spine on its head. The tip of the spine glows or wiggles, so it works like a fishing rod with bait on the end.
explain: The name comes from «angler», a person who fishes with a rod. So when you read «an anglerfish dangles a glowing lure in front of its mouth like a fishing rod», you can picture a fish that fishes. The lure is the glowing bait at the end of the spine.
explain: Context gives you clues again: «Anglerfish teeth point inwards so prey cannot escape.» Prey are animals hunted for food, and the teeth tell you the anglerfish is a hunter. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: An anglerfish has a glowing lure on its head to attract prey.
fact: A «lure» is bait that draws an animal in, and here the bait is a light.
fact: The light in the lure is made by bacteria, tiny living things. Scientists call this bioluminescence.
fact: Many anglerfish live in the deep, dark ocean, where food is rare.
fact: In some kinds, the tiny male fuses onto the much larger female for life.
exercise: «A female deep-sea anglerfish has a glowing lure on her head.» What is the lure? | The fish's tail fin | *The glowing bait on a long spine | A type of deep-sea shark | A kind of seaweed
exercise: «So the deep is full of clever tricks.» What does deep mean here? | *The deep sea, the dark part of the ocean | A type of fishing rod | Shallow water near the beach | Very hungry
exercise: The name anglerfish comes from «angler», a person who fishes with a rod. Why is it a good name? | It lives in a river | It has long wings | It can walk on land | *It fishes with a glowing lure, like an angler with a rod
test: In «Anglerfish teeth point inwards so prey cannot escape», which word means animals hunted for food? | Escape | Inwards | *Prey | Teeth
test: The light in the lure is made by bacteria. What does bioluminescence mean? | *Light made by living things | A fishing rod | Dark water in the deep sea | Sharp teeth
exam: In «an anglerfish dangles a glowing lure», what does dangles mean? | Sleeps quietly | Bites hard | *Hangs loosely and swings | Swims very fast
